# XAUlytics ETL Developer Rule

- Build ETL code in Python 3.12+ with a clean module layout (`extract`, `transform`, `load`, `config`, `logging`).
- Keep runtime Linux-friendly for Ubuntu-based Docker and GitHub Actions; avoid OS-specific paths and shell behavior.
- Read configuration only from environment variables (no hardcoded secrets). Use clear required vars and fail fast when missing.
- Store production secrets (for example `SUPABASE_URL`, `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`, `METALPRICEAPI_KEY`) in GitHub Actions Secrets only.
- For development runs, load secrets from local environment variables; values may be sourced from Windows Credential Manager and injected into the environment at runtime.
- Treat MetalpriceAPI as the source of truth for daily metal prices. Normalize API payloads to deterministic schemas and UTC dates.
- Minimize MetalpriceAPI usage: only request data needed for each run (daily, historical, symbols) and respect rate limits appropriate to your API plan.
- Daily ingestion uses `/v1/yesterday` (prior UTC calendar day); support explicit historical loads for user-specified dates or ranges (backfill/repair).
- Configure spot bases with `METALPRICEAPI_BASE_CURRENCIES` (comma-separated; default when unset is USD only). One MetalpriceAPI spot request per base per run. Optional OHLC via `METALPRICEAPI_ENABLE_OHLC`.
- Enforce unit conventions in transformations: precious metals use troy ounces, non-precious metals use ounces.
- Design ETL to be idempotent so reruns do not duplicate records; upsert on `(pricing_date, quote_code, base_currency)`.
- Load into Supabase using explicit table contracts, typed records, and retry handling for transient network/API failures.
- Add structured logging for each ETL phase with run metadata (run id, source date, row counts, load status, errors).
- Validate data before load (required fields, numeric parsing, date checks) and quarantine/skip invalid rows with diagnostics.
- Keep functions small and testable; separate pure transforms from I/O for straightforward unit tests.
- Include smoke-test and dry-run entrypoints so CI can validate extract/transform without writing production data.
- Prepare for daily scheduler execution: single command entrypoint, deterministic exit codes, and no interactive prompts.
- Provide required MetalpriceAPI attribution in documentation and any page/view that displays MetalpriceAPI-derived data. Use exactly:
  - Text: `Powered by <a href="https://metalpriceapi.com/" title="Free Precious Metal Rates API">MetalpriceAPI.com</a>`
  - Image: `<a href="https://metalpriceapi.com/" title="Free Precious Metal Rates API"><img src='https://metalpriceapi.com/logo-dark.png' alt="Precious metal data by MetalpriceAPI.com" border="0" height="26"></a>`